  "body": "Southwest Lower Michigan shows peak color at 100 percent modeled coverage, while Southeast Lower trails at 79 percent in the falling phase. All other regions remain early in the season at 7 percent, except Central and Saginaw Bay at 14 percent falling. The contrast reflects significant variation across the state.\n\nRain is expected across all regions over the next few days, with highs ranging from 62 to 70 degrees and lows from 33 to 40. This moisture and cool overnight temperatures may accelerate leaf drop in advanced areas while supporting color development in early-stage regions. Weekend conditions favor viewing in drier windows between rain events.\n\nFor peak foliage this weekend, Blue Star Highway along the Saugatuck dunes in Southwest Lower offers the best current display. Those in Southeast Lower can explore the Irish Hills along US-12 for strong falling-phase color. Northern regions remain too early for significant color but provide scenic drives for those prioritizing landscape over foliage.",
